/* Introduction to C Language:
   -------------------------
      C language was developed by "Dennis Ritchie" in the year 1972 at
AT & T Bell laboratories in USA. C is also as "Structured Language".

C Character Set:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Alphabets : Both Upper case and Lower case

Numbers   : 0 to 9

Special Symbols : ~, @, !, $, %, ^, &, *

C Tokens:
---------
1. Keywords
2. Identifiers
3. Constants
4. Variables
5. Operators

1. Keywords:
	All keyword have fixed meanings and these meanings
 cannot be changed.Keywords are building block of the program.
There are 32 keywords in C. They are,

auto
break
case
char
const
continue
default
do
double
else
enum
extern
float
for
goto
if
int
long
register
return
short
signed
sizeof
static
struct
switch
typedef
union
unsigned
void
volatile
while

2. Identifier:
	Identifier refers to the names of variable, functions and arrays.

3. Constants:
	Constants in C refers to fixed values that do not change during the
execution  of the program.

Types of Constants:
a) Integer constant
b) Real constant
c) Sigle character constant
d) String constant

a) Integer constant:
	  An integer constant refers to a sequence of digits.
Ex:
	434
	545564
	3
	+546
	-45
b) Real constants:
	These are represented by numbers containing fractional parts like
34.456
23.00

c) Single character constant:
	A single character constant contains a single character enclosed
within single quotes.

Ex:
	'j'      'k'

d) String character constant:
	It is a sequence of characters enclosed with in double quotes.
Ex:
	"ifc"        "5345"   "#$$$"

4. Variables:
	A variable is a data name that may be used to store a data value.
It remains changed during the execution of the program.

Ex:
	name
	table_name
	x_1


Compiler:
	It is used to compile the program. (Alt+F9)
	To run the program - Ctrl+F9
	To save the program - F2      Programname.c
	To close the Edit Screen - Alt+X

*/

/*
Header Files:
#include<stdio.h> - Standard Input Output Header file.
#include<conio.h> - Console Input Output Header file.

Name        Datatypes   Control String
------           ---------   --------------
Integer       	int	       %d
Float           float	       %f
Character       char           %c
String	        char	       %s

Input Statement:
----------------
scanf("Control String",var_name);

Output Statement:
-----------------
printf("Statement");
printf("Control String",var_name);
*/



